{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R93kohVnXU3NK6LQ9h2KtG","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel02.2-uc001-head\n     2→title: \"Print the first lines or bytes of files via head\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator invokes the Go head binary to extract the beginning of files or pipeline\n     6→  output. The differential testing harness runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew\n     7→  reference binary (ghead from coreutils) with the same arguments, stdin, and environment,\n     8→  then compares stdout byte-for-byte.\n     9→\n    10→actor: Human Operator\n    11→\n    12→trigger: |\n    13→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd018-head.yaml) and invokes do-work to\n    14→  produce a passing differential test for cmd/head.\n    15→\n    16→flow:\n    17→  - id: F1\n    18→    step: |\n    19→      The operator runs \"seq 1 20 | ./bin/head\". head prints the first 10 lines\n    20→      (the default count) to stdout.\n    21→  - id: F2\n    22→    step: |\n    23→      The operator runs \"seq 1 20 | ./bin/head -n 5\" to print only the first 5 lines.\n    24→  - id: F3\n    25→    step: |\n    26→      The operator runs \"seq 1 20 | ./bin/head -n -5\" to print all lines except the\n    27→      last 5 (lines 1 through 15).\n    28→  - id: F4\n    29→    step: |\n    30→      The operator runs \"printf 'abcdefghij' | ./bin/head -c 5\" to print the first\n    31→      5 bytes.\n    32→  - id: F5\n    33→    step: |\n    34→      The operator runs \"./bin/head file1.txt file2.txt\" to test multi-file output\n    35→      with headers in the format \"==> FILENAME <==\".\n    36→  - id: F6\n    37→    step: |\n    38→      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/head and\n    39→      ghead with the same arguments and environment.\n    40→  - id: F7\n    41→    step: |\n    42→      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte and exit codes. Both binaries must\n    43→      produce identical output.\n    44→\n    45→touchpoints:\n    46→  - T1: \"cmd/head — line-count, byte-count, negative counts, multi-file headers, quiet/verbose (prd018-head R1, R2, R3, R4)\"\n    47→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, stdout comparison\"\n    48→\n    49→success_criteria:\n    50→  - id: S1\n    51→    criterion: cmd/head compiles and ./bin/head exists after mage build.\n    52→  - id: S2\n    53→    criterion: |\n    54→      \"seq 1 20 | ./bin/head\" produces lines 1 through 10, matching ghead.\n    55→  - id: S3\n    56→    criterion: |\n    57→      Explicit line count works: \"head -n 5\" produces exactly 5 lines.\n    58→  - id: S4\n    59→    criterion: |\n    60→      Negative line count works: \"head -n -5\" prints all lines except the last 5.\n    61→  - id: S5\n    62→    criterion: |\n    63→      Byte count works: \"head -c 5\" prints exactly 5 bytes.\n    64→  - id: S6\n    65→    criterion: |\n    66→      Multi-file headers are printed in the format \"==> FILENAME <==\", matching ghead.\n    67→  - id: S7\n    68→    criterion: |\n    69→      Header suppression (-q) and forced headers (-v) work correctly.\n    70→  - id: S8\n    71→    criterion: |\n    72→      Error handling works: non-existent file produces stderr error, exits 1, and\n    73→      remaining files are still processed.\n    74→  - id: S9\n    75→    criterion: |\n    76→      The differential test passes for default, -n, -c, negative counts, multi-file,\n    77→      -q, -v, stdin, and error cases.\n    78→\n    79→out_of_scope:\n    80→  - Zero-terminated line mode (-z) is excluded per the PRD.\n    81→  - Decimal multiplier suffixes (kB, MB, GB) are excluded per the PRD.\n    82→\n    83→test_suite: test-rel02.2\n    84→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d4c178c-c666-4b39-b0d2-ff47d37e3168","uuid":"8e5e3233-6b84-4873-a435-38025e369836","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/343/docs/specs/use-cases/rel02.2-uc001-head.yaml","content":"id: rel02.2-uc001-head\ntitle: \"Print the first lines or bytes of files via head\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator invokes the Go head binary to extract the beginning of files or pipeline\n  output. The differential testing harness runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew\n  reference binary (ghead from coreutils) with the same arguments, stdin, and environment,\n  then compares stdout byte-for-byte.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd018-head.yaml) and invokes do-work to\n  produce a passing differential test for cmd/head.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs \"seq 1 20 | ./bin/head\". head prints the first 10 lines\n      (the default count) to stdout.\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      The operator runs \"seq 1 20 | ./bin/head -n 5\" to print only the first 5 lines.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      The operator runs \"seq 1 20 | ./bin/head -n -5\" to print all lines except the\n      last 5 (lines 1 through 15).\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The operator runs \"printf 'abcdefghij' | ./bin/head -c 5\" to print the first\n      5 bytes.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The operator runs \"./bin/head file1.txt file2.txt\" to test multi-file output\n      with headers in the format \"==> FILENAME <==\".\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/head and\n      ghead with the same arguments and environment.\n  - id: F7\n    step: |\n      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte and exit codes. Both binaries must\n      produce identical output.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/head — line-count, byte-count, negative counts, multi-file headers, quiet/verbose (prd018-head R1, R2, R3, R4)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, stdout comparison\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/head compiles and ./bin/head exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: |\n      \"seq 1 20 | ./bin/head\" produces lines 1 through 10, matching ghead.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: |\n      Explicit line count works: \"head -n 5\" produces exactly 5 lines.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: |\n      Negative line count works: \"head -n -5\" prints all lines except the last 5.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: |\n      Byte count works: \"head -c 5\" prints exactly 5 bytes.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: |\n      Multi-file headers are printed in the format \"==> FILENAME <==\", matching ghead.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: |\n      Header suppression (-q) and forced headers (-v) work correctly.\n  - id: S8\n    criterion: |\n      Error handling works: non-existent file produces stderr error, exits 1, and\n      remaining files are still processed.\n  - id: S9\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test passes for default, -n, -c, negative counts, multi-file,\n      -q, -v, stdin, and error cases.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - Zero-terminated line mode (-z) is excluded per the PRD.\n  - Decimal multiplier suffixes (kB, MB, GB) are excluded per the PRD.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel02.2\n","numLines":84,"startLine":1,"totalLines":84}}}
